File Index

Sub-components + hooks for AutoLevelingWizard.tsx (the wizard that replaces AutoLevelingModal).

/useCharacterLevel.ts
Purpose: useCharacterLogin() — the connected character's level + name from GMCP login_data (game:character-login event + __SA_EVENT_SNAPSHOTS__ for late subscribers).

/useWizardDraft.ts
Purpose: useWizardDraft() — in-memory wizard draft (areaSlug, area detail, DraftTarget[], mode, playerClass, initiationCommand, buffs, fightCommands, playerAlignment — default 'neutral'; the MOB's alignment is engine-detected from auras, not in the draft; startRoom — 2026-09-12, an editable Review-step reminder seeded from area.startRoom, purely informational; restStartOfRound/restEndOfRound — semicolon-separated command text, 2026-09-12 — + restDuringRound: AutoLevelRestDuringRoundRule[]; weightAtOrAbovePct/weightCommands — 2026-09-13, weightCommands also semicolon-separated text, no separate enable flag — a blank weightCommands list IS off, the checkbox was dropped same day per live-playtest feedback) + actions (setArea, toggleTarget, addCustomTarget, removeCustomTarget, patch, reset). Not persisted until Start builds the AutoLevelConfig.
Context (2026-11-13): target rows are identified by targetRowId (area: normalized ORIGINAL room line; custom: stored record id), not by lookName, because an edit changes the room line; toggleTarget/editTarget/removeCustomTarget take that id. addCustomTarget refuses a line already shown by any row, including the original line of an edited or hidden area row. unmatchedOverrides rides in the draft next to the rows. Hiding a row sets enabled:false AND persists hidden; the per-run checkbox is not persisted, and draftToConfig reads only `enabled`.

/AreaStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 1 — area list from autoleveling-content.getAreaIndex() grouped by continent, search box, a min/max Level range gate (seeded ±5 from GMCP level once, then user-owned; areasForLevelRange overlaps with a ±4 margin and drops "range not set" areas), level-match dot + in-band L-range highlight when connected, ★ for IsExcellentLevelingArea, per-row L-range/steps/targets ("level range not set" when span ≥ 40), "Custom path…" fallthrough row.

/TargetsStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 2 — recommended targets (from the area detail) pre-checked with level badge + kill keyword; separate "Your targets" list for user additions; manual add row (look description + kill keyword). Toggle/add/remove flow up to the wizard which persists customs to autoleveling-user-data.
Context (2026-11-13): the Targets step is also the editor for the PLAYER'S personal overrides of pre-loaded area targets. Rows are identified by targetRowId (area: the normalized ORIGINAL room line; custom: the stored record id), never by the room line, because the room line is what an edit changes. The step validates text (empty, over 200, ";" or line breaks, a room line another row or a hidden row's original line already uses) BEFORE asking the wizard to save, and shows the wizard's message if the save fails. Hide is persisted (a row under "Hidden by you", never enabled); the checkbox is per-run and not persisted. Unmatched edits (target left the served list) are listed with a delete the player must click. Behaviour and storage: docs/game/autopilot.md. Tests: TargetsStep.test.tsx, and AutoLevelingWizard.targets.test.tsx for the real wizard + storage flow.

/CombatStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 3 — class selector (served catalog via getClassCatalog(), base classes then a "Reclasses" optgroup, DSL_CLASSES_FALLBACK only if the catalog is empty → setPrefs + reloads that class's fight overlay), read-only level/name from useCharacterLogin, engage-command input, one Good/Neutral/Evil "Your alignment" AlignPick (persists via setPrefs; the mob's alignment is read live from auras by the engine), a pre-round buff editor and a per-class fight-command rotation. 2026-09-13 rewrite of both catalog pickers: both use `FilterableSelect` (typeahead, alphabetized, replaces the native `<select>`+`<optgroup>`). First pass had the buff picker show a hardcoded BUFF_CATALOG unconditionally alongside the class's own group-filtered spells (leaking e.g. Shukenja-only spells into every class's list) — fixed, then REPLACED entirely same day: the buff picker now shows every ability the selected class actually has (`abilitiesForClass`, no group filtering), grouped by type (Skills/Spells/Songs headers) — no more generic catalog fallback, no more group-heuristic guessing which abilities count as "buffs" (that heuristic kept being wrong; see autoleveling-classes.ts's `.annotated`). `addClassBuff` still cross-references BUFF_CATALOG by name for a verified cmd+affect when available; otherwise seeds an `unverified: true` guess — a skill guesses a bare command + tick-gate (skills rarely register a GMCP affect), a spell/song guesses `cast '<name>'` + an affect-name gate. Fight section's "Add ability" picker (classOffensiveAbilities → skill = bare name, spell = `cast '<name>' {name}`, UNCHANGED — still group-filtered) got the same FilterableSelect + alphabetize treatment — 2026-09-12: pre-fills cooldownSec from autoleveling-user-data's getLearnedCooldown(cmd) instead of always 0. 3-way gate segmented control per buff (affect drops / every N ticks / every round) + affect-gated inCombatCmd + holdNearLevel unchanged. 2026-09-12 additions on every buff card AND fight-command row (the latter restructured from a bare .editorRow into a .buffCard so there's room): shared `VitalsGateControl` (checkbox + hp/mp/stamina dropdown + below/above toggle + %% input → BuffRow/FightRow.vitalsGate) and `OnceGateControl` (no limit / once per round / once per fight → .onceKey). Debounce-saves to autoleveling-user-data; the wizard seeds the draft from those stores on area selection. 2026-09-13: added `ReorderButtons` (shared ↑/↓ `.iconButton` pair) to every buff card and fight-command row — `moveItem()` swaps the row with its adjacent neighbor and re-commits the array, since execution order IS list order (buffs cast top-to-bottom in `steps.start.pre`, fight commands sent top-to-bottom in `steps.fight.exec` — see `draftToConfig`) and there was previously no way to change it without deleting and re-adding rows. Saves go through the private useDebouncedSave: a burst of edits becomes ONE write of the latest rows per 500 ms, and an edit still pending when the step unmounts is flushed at once instead of dropped; the latest save callback is tracked in a layout effect (a render-time ref write trips react-hooks/refs). With no areaSlug the step renders only a "pick an area" message, so the `if (areaSlug)` guards in the commit helpers are defensive, not reachable from the UI. Tests: CombatStep.test.tsx (mocks the user-data and class-catalog modules).
Context (2026-11-13): CombatStep PRE-FILLS buffs and fight commands for the chosen class (autoleveling-class-defaults.ts: verified BUFF_CATALOG rows for abilities the class has at the character's level, up to 3 fight commands) ONLY when nothing was ever saved: buffs are per area, fight per area+class, read with the *OrNull getters where null = never saved and [] = saved empty. A saved set, even an emptied one, always wins; rows already in the draft are never replaced; seeded rows live in the draft and are written only on the first edit (SETTINGS-06). Two paths, one decision per area|class (seededFor ref): the mount effect (remembered class) and onChangeClass (a newer pick wins via classReq; buffs follow the new class while none are saved). A pending seed is dropped on unmount or when a newer class decision moved seededFor. An empty class catalog shows a notice (catalogLoaded) instead of silently listing the 5-name DSL_CLASSES_FALLBACK. Tests: CombatStep.test.tsx (saves, pausing), CombatStep.prefill.test.tsx (pre-fill, class pick, list, help). Pausing a fight command (FightRow.disabled, 2026-11-13): the row keeps cooldown/gates/order and is saved with the list, but draftToConfig drops it from steps.fight.exec so the engine never sends it; Resume DELETES the key so a resumed row is stored like one never paused. The default pre-fill never pauses a fight command. BUFFS differ: a default buff the class only gets at a LATER level is seeded PAUSED (BuffRow.disabled) so it is visible but never cast, and buffAbilityNote shows a render-time warning (computed from the catalog and the character's level, never stored, so it follows level-ups) only while the row's command is still the verified `cast`: once the player changes it to a potion/wand/staff they have defined how to apply it and the warning goes. A buff the class never gets is not seeded. setBuffGate now calls buffRowForGate (autoleveling-class-defaults.ts), which SPREADS the row and removes only the old mode's own fields (affect, refreshTicks, inCombatCmd, holdNearLevel), so a field added to BuffRow survives a mode switch by default (SETTINGS-07); it used to be rebuilt from named fields and lost vitalsGate and onceKey. The test lists every BuffRow field as Required<BuffRow>, so a new field fails to compile until it is listed.

/FilterableSelect.tsx
Purpose: New 2026-09-13 — a text-input typeahead that behaves like a `<select>` for the caller (one `onPick(value)` on commit) but filters a flat option list live-as-you-type instead of a native dropdown; consecutive options sharing a `group` get one header, mirroring `<optgroup>`. Callers alphabetize before passing options in (this component preserves given order). Used by CombatStep.tsx's buff-add and fight-command-add pickers. A group header is decided against the FILTERED list (the previous shown option's group), so the first shown option always gets its header even when the filter hid the start of its group; reading a variable mutated during render did the same job but trips react-hooks/immutability. Gotcha: the highlight resets to the first option whenever the query or the open state changes, so ArrowDown on a CLOSED list opens it with the first option highlighted (not the second). Tests: FilterableSelect.test.tsx.

/RestStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 4 (new, 2026-09-12) — Rest. Two plain-text fields (restStartOfRound "wake up", restEndOfRound "rest", both semicolon-separated for multiple commands, same join convention as fullRoute) + a repeatable during-round rule card (HP/MP/Stamina ≤ threshold, all optional and AND'd together per rule — the user's own example is "HP below 50% AND mana below 50%" — plus a recover-to ≥ target per stat), reusing the buff-card/gateBar styling from CombatStep. All rest behavior is out-of-combat only, enforced by the engine (autoleveling-engine.ts checkDuringRoundRest), not this UI. 2026-09-13 (live-playtest fix): both fields now go through the alias/script "command processor" (RuntimeSingleton.Runtime.executeAlias, via a new deps.sendThroughCommandProcessor), not a raw literal send — a rest sequence built as the player's own alias/macro was being sent to the MUD verbatim and silently doing nothing. Same convention now applies to the during-round rules below since they reuse these exact two fields.

/WeightStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 5 (new, 2026-09-13) — Weight, between Rest and Review. Two unconditional fields: a threshold-percentage number input and a semicolon-separated commands text field, same convention as Rest's fields. NO enable checkbox (removed same day, live-playtest feedback: "not a simple checkbox") — a blank commands field IS off, same convention Rest's own start/end-of-round fields already used. Out-of-combat only, enforced by the engine (autoleveling-engine.ts checkWeightGate — gates on `commands.length`, not a separate flag), not this UI — fires the drop sequence once per threshold crossing (edge-triggered).

/ReviewStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 6 (was step 5 before WeightStep was inserted, 2026-09-13; step 4 before RestStep, 2026-09-12) — mostly read-only plain-language summary of the draft (area + level range + ★, an editable "Start room" reminder text field seeded from area.startRoom, fullRoute() step count with a "Show steps" disclosure listing every command — explicit `{i+1}.` text rather than a native `<ol>`, whose counter rendered wrong inside the scrolling container, cause not fully diagnosed — enabled/total targets as a collapsible `{lookName} ({engageName})` list, class, alignment row (no "you" prefix — just the alignment + the aura-detection note), engage command, buff list with per-row gate/in-combat/hold-near-level via describeBuffGate() + an "unverified" flag, fight-command list with cooldowns, a Rest row summarizing both command lists + every during-round rule in plain language, a Weight row ("drop at N% carry weight: <commands>" or "off"), mode + loop). No config is built here — that happens on Start.

Context (2026-11-18): the Route row has an "edit route" editor (textarea, steps separated by `;` or new lines) shown only when the wizard passes onSaveRoute; it only asks, AutoLevelingWizard stores (setRouteOverride) and patches draft.area.dirs. draft.routeDefaultDirs keeps the served route for the "Shared route: N steps" hint and reset. Escape inside the textarea cancels the edit only (stopPropagation) so the window stays open.

/dsl-classes.ts
Purpose: DSL_CLASSES_FALLBACK — just the 5 base class names, a last-resort static list for CombatStep's class picker when the served catalog (autoleveling-classes) is unreachable AND its offline JSON is empty. The real list comes from GET /maps/autoleveling/classes.

/TargetsHelp.tsx
Purpose: In-step help for the Targets step (the blue (i) swaps the step body for this article, same pattern as MapHelp). End-user text: pre-loaded vs your own targets, edit / hide / reset, unmatched edits, the text rules, and how edits move to another device (Save/Load to cloud). Keep it in step with TargetsStep and docs/game/autopilot.md.

/CombatHelp.tsx
Purpose: In-step help for the Combat step (blue (i), same pattern as TargetsHelp): the class list, what is filled in for you and when, what you keep. Keep it in step with autoleveling-class-defaults.ts (DEFAULT_BUFF_LABELS, DEFAULT_FIGHT_ROWS) and docs/game/autopilot.md.


/TargetsStep.tsx (Escape)
Purpose: (gotcha) the inline row editor stops Escape from propagating when it cancels an edit; the Autopilot window around it also closes on Escape through hooks/useWindowLayer, so without the stop one press would cancel the edit and close the window.

/FilterableSelect.tsx (Escape)
Purpose: (gotcha) stops Escape from propagating only while its list is open; with the list closed the key goes on to close the window around it.

CombatStep.tsx (2026-11-18, live findings): every buff card and fight row also carries CombatStateControl (combatState), EnemyGateControl (enemyGate, phrases from autoleveling-enemy-condition.ts shown as "about N%") and, for affect buffs, the retry checkbox (retryUntilSet, only ever stored as false). updateBuff/updateFight strip undefined values so a cleared option is truly absent from the stored row; unresolvedNote flags a command with a placeholder left (the engine refuses to send it). Tests: CombatStep.options.test.tsx, CombatStep.gates.test.tsx.
